<!-- Authored for test_projects/topdownplatformer; edit it in Tiled.

     100x30 tiles at 16px = 1600x480 pixels, a meadow walled with trees and
     crossed west to east along row 15, y 248. Every gap runs from row 1 to row
     28, on the `pits` layer in tiles of class `gap` from pits.tsx: trenches one
     tile wide in columns 16, 20 and 24, a chasm in columns 34 to 49 (x 544 to
     800), and one in columns 58 to 81 (x 928 to 1312).

     The `platforms` layer lies under `spawns`, which is marked `actors`, so a
     hero draws over the raft they ride and sorts against what stands in
     `spawns`. In `platforms`, `shuttle` is a polyline of class `Raft` that
     its centre walks back and forth, stopping 12 px short of each bank, and
     `ring` a polygon it walks round, never touching a bank. The ring's west
     and east legs run 12 px from a bank. Each carries its size in its
     deck_width and deck_height properties.

     In `spawns`, `start` is where the first hero stands. `first`, `second`
     and `last` are points of class `Flag`, `crate` of class `Crate` and
     `walker` of class `Walker`, which rides the ring. -->
